# Overrides for ./scripts/test-all.sh. Copy to .env.test-all (git-ignored).
#
# Every value shown is the script's own default, so uncomment only what actually
# differs — an override that merely repeats the default is a second copy of the
# same number, and the two drift. That is not hypothetical: TYPECHECK_BASELINE
# sat at 203 here, 205 in this file and 195 in the script while the real count
# was 197, which left the typecheck gate admitting six new errors in silence.
#
# Development happens on one machine (the dev VPS), so a value set here is not a
# personal preference others will differ from — it is the configuration. Prefer
# fixing the default in test-all.sh over shadowing it.

# --- Paths -------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRONTEND_DIR defaults to the repo containing this script.
#FRONTEND_DIR=/home/you/git/clinic-cms/skcms
#BACKEND_DIR=/home/you/git/clinic-cms/backend

# --- Docker ------------------------------------------------------------------
#COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose-development.yml
#COMPOSE_CMD="docker compose"
#BACKEND_TEST_SERVICE=fastapi     # container that runs pytest
#BACKEND_SHELL_SERVICE=django     # container that runs manage.py shell
#BACKEND_WORKDIR=/app
#NEO4J_SERVICE=neo4j
#NEO4J_CONTAINER=backend-neo4j-1  # `docker inspect` name for the healthcheck

# --- Frontend ----------------------------------------------------------------
#PKG_MANAGER=pnpm
#DEV_SERVER_PORT=3000             # the `pnpm dev` server nginx maps dev.<site> to
#E2E_STOP_DEV_SERVER=0            # 1 stops it for the run and starts it after.
                                  # Leave 0 when running the `sites` project: it
                                  # browses dev.<site>, so stopping the server
                                  # serves the [fallback] page instead and the
                                  # specs fail as though the pages were broken.

# --- Timeouts (seconds) ------------------------------------------------------
#NEO4J_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=180         # neo4j needs ~40s from cold
#STACK_WAIT_TIMEOUT=300

# --- Behaviour ---------------------------------------------------------------
#SKIP_BACKEND=0                   # 1 skips the slow pytest suite
#SKIP_FRONTEND=0
#SEED_BDD_USERS=1                 # seed per-role users before the BDD suite
#TYPECHECK_BASELINE=197           # fail only if svelte-check errors exceed this.
                                  # Keep it equal to the count in test-all.sh, and
                                  # lower both as the backlog is paid down — a
                                  # baseline above the real count silently admits
                                  # that many new errors.
#PYTEST_ARGS=-m "not integration" # narrow the backend run

# --- Parallelism -------------------------------------------------------------
# How many BDD scenarios run at once. Set it to E2E_WORKERS: one playwright
# worker per worker SITE, each owning one outright.
#
# Never MORE than E2E_WORKERS. A site is not shareable -- SEED_TAG derives from
# it and the cleanup helpers delete by that tag -- so two workers on one site
# means one scenario's teardown destroys another's data mid-run. workerSlot()
# throws rather than let that happen, so an over-large number fails loudly.
# To go faster, seed more sites.
#
# The other ceiling is MEMORY, not cores: the E2E_WORKERS vite servers are all
# resident before a single browser starts (~230MB each), and every playwright
# worker is a chromium on top. One that loses the race dies mid-step, and the
# failure reads as "Target crashed" or as an assertion whose Received is
# undefined — a fact about the box, not about the app. If timeouts climb while
# the pass count stalls, this number is too high.
#
# Measured: 8 sites + 8 browsers ran 136 scenarios in 4.9 minutes on
# 12 cores / 32GB, load ~5.
#PLAYWRIGHT_WORKERS=8

# The number of worker SITES. Half are served under a base path and half at
# their root, and ONE chromium project spans them all -- a worker exercises
# whichever shape its own site has, so both shapes are covered in a single pass.
# Splitting the pool by shape instead capped parallelism at half the sites,
# because playwright runs projects one after another rather than interleaving.
#
# The old description, kept for the shape detail: the lower half is served
# at the root, the upper half under a base path, and the two chromium projects
# run every scenario against both. Must stay even, and raising it needs matching
# rows in scripts/nginx/e2e-workers.conf plus /etc/hosts entries.
#E2E_WORKERS=8

# Retry a failed scenario once, so trace: 'on-first-retry' produces a trace.
# 0 halves the wall clock of a run you already know is red and are iterating on;
# leave it at 1 for a run whose failures you will need to diagnose.
#PLAYWRIGHT_RETRIES=1
